# Line-ending policy.
#
# Windows' default (core.autocrlf=true) converts everything to CRLF on checkout,
# which breaks two things in this repository:
#
#   1. benchmarks/simulator/adb is a POSIX `sh` shim. A CRLF shebang line makes
#      it unrunnable on Linux and macOS, which is where CI runs.
#   2. Normalising once here stops every cross-platform checkout from showing
#      the entire tree as modified.
#
# Store LF in the repository; check out LF everywhere except Windows batch files.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files must be CRLF to be executed by cmd.exe.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The POSIX adb shim is executed by sh and must keep LF.
benchmarks/simulator/adb text eol=lf

# Binary assets are left alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
